wands in the hands of monsters are a real threat.  Once you start
getting high enough level or deep enough in the dungeon where @
monsters start being generated you should consider each of them a
potential carrier of an attack wand.  Not to say that those are the
only monsters that carry/use wands, just saying that if you don't have
reflection or the appropriate resistances at that point, you could be
in for a one-turn death.

Like sjdevnull said, pets are useful.  If your hypothetical large dog
had encountered the elf first you might have ended up carrying the
wand of sleep rather than being on the business end of it.  Sure pets
take more time to herd and manage, but it can be less time-consuming
than starting a new game.  It's a judgement call and it's up to you
how conservatively to play but careful/slow play is far more likely to
ascend than speedy play.

You don't have to keep all of your pets with you, just tame the ones
that you see but maybe only keep 2 with you.  If you find a polytrap
later, you can go back and collect the feral ones and try to get an
uber-pet.


